\ port/lab/compile.4 - a front end for a design's compiler: relf's shell
\ compiled the way relf's own compiler compiles it.
\
\ Why. A design runs the lab's Forth benchmarks faster than relf, and relfsh
\ two to three times slower (Iteration 941). Counted on the knee's loop.sh:
\ 57.4 million dispatches to relf's 15.2 million, 10.4 million of them calls
\ to relf's 0.97 million. A design's speed is in its image: the lab's
\ converter (tools/layout.py) specialises the kernel's call sites, gives
\ variables their slot opcodes, folds and fuses. Code compiled at run time
\ gets none of that - the kernel's compiler calls every word but its thirty
\ primitives: a variable is a call to DOVAR (4.1 million on loop.sh), a
\ constant a call to LIT EXIT, CELLS or 2DUP or - or +! a call to a colon
\ word (2.9 million). The benchmarks are mostly primitives; the shell is not.
\ relf's compiler has VAR@, constants as literals, its primitives inline.
\
\ So COMPILE, here, which the interpreter (interp.4) calls:
\   - a variable or a CREATEd word (its code DOVAR): its address, a literal;
\   - a constant: its value, a literal;
\   - a kernel word that is a few primitives (CELLS, -, 2DUP, +!, ...): those
\     primitives, inline - the kernel's own definitions, copied;
\   - words registered later (after.4): BUFFER:'s and DEFER's children.
\ An address literal is an absolute address, and a saved image loads
\ elsewhere each run (START moves): every such site is recorded, the save
\ keeps the list (lab/save.4), and PORT-BOOT moves each by START's change
\ before anything else runs. After boot this is off - a forth command's
\ definitions are the kernel compiler's, as before.
\   - and a colon word of at most INL-MAX tokens, none of them immediate
\     or the return stack's: its tokens, compiled again in its place (as
\     relf's inliner does its small words).
\ Nothing here knows a design's encoding: the DOVAR byte and where a
\ literal's cell lies are found by compiling probes. Loaded right after
\ port/relf.4; interp.4's INTERPRET calls this COMPILE, from again.4 on (the
\ files up to there are read by the kernel's interpreter, and compiled by
\ the kernel's COMPILE,).
\
\ And on a design with the JIT (PORT-JIT, build.sh's): its JIT translates a
\ word only if it can translate every word below it, and on the shell it
\ took almost nothing - fastest-x86-64 interpreted 32.8 million dispatches
\ of loop.sh. A few words it has no stencil for (the kernel's variables,
\ the system call, its SCAN, HERE, PAD) left every word above them
\ interpreted. So, below: the kernel's variables as literals too; a call
\ through EXECUTE (the gene jitexec) of a word the JIT refuses but which
\ does not throw, and of a word too deep for it; PORT-BOOT left to the
\ interpreter. jitwords.4 has the string words and the rest as the JIT takes
\ them.

BASE @  DECIMAL

: OLD-COMPILE, ( xt --- )  COMPILE, ;            \ the kernel's

\ ---- the probes -----------------------------------------------------
VARIABLE PROBE-V
' PROBE-V C@ CONSTANT DOVAR-BYTE                 \ a variable's first code byte
VARIABLE REL-OK   0 REL-OK !
: PROBE-LIT [ PROBE-V ] LITERAL [ HERE 1 CELLS - @ PROBE-V = REL-OK ! ] ;   \ a cell, at the end
1 CELLS 4 / 1+ CONSTANT CELL-SHIFT              \ CELLS's: 3, or 2 on a 32-bit design

\ ---- the build's memory: one block of the host's, not saved ----------
VARIABLE SP-HP   0 SP-HP !   VARIABLE SP-END   0 SP-END !
: SP-ALLOT ( u --- a-addr )
  SP-HP @ SWAP SP-HP +!  SP-HP @ SP-END @ U> ABORT" compile.4: its memory is full" ;

\ ---- the sites ------------------------------------------------------
VARIABLE REL-ON    0 REL-ON !                    \ this front end at work
VARIABLE REL-REC   0 REL-REC !                   \ recording sites (the build)
VARIABLE VAR-LIT   0 VAR-LIT !                   \ variables as literals (RELOCATE's own: not)
VARIABLE RS-TAB    0 RS-TAB !                    \ the sites: START offsets, a cell each
VARIABLE RS-N      0 RS-N !
262144 CONSTANT RS-MAX
: RS-ADD ( a-addr --- )
  RS-N @ RS-MAX < 0= ABORT" compile.4: too many address literals"
  START @ -  RS-TAB @ RS-N @ CELLS + !  1 RS-N +! ;
16777216 CONSTANT IMAGE-SPAN                     \ an address within START and this is the image's
: IN-IMAGE? ( x --- f )  START @ - IMAGE-SPAN U< ;
: REL-LITERAL ( x --- )   \ a literal; an address in the image, a site
  DUP POSTPONE LITERAL
  DUP IN-IMAGE? REL-REC @ AND IF
    HERE 1 CELLS - @ OVER = 0= ABORT" compile.4: a literal's bytes are not where the probe found them"
    HERE 1 CELLS - RS-ADD
  THEN DROP ;

\ The image's list (lab/save.4 writes it): the count, then each site's
\ distance from the one before, seven bits a byte, the top bit set on
\ every byte but a number's last.
VARIABLE RS-IMG    0 RS-IMG !                     \ its START offset, 0 for none
VARIABLE RS-START  0 RS-START !                   \ START when it was saved
: RS-VARINT, ( u --- )
  BEGIN DUP 127 U> WHILE DUP 127 AND 128 OR C, 7 RSHIFT REPEAT C, ;
: RS-WRITE ( --- )    \ into the dictionary, before the save
  HERE START @ - RS-IMG !  START @ RS-START !
  RS-N @ ,  0                                     ( prev )
  RS-N @ 0 ?DO
    RS-TAB @ I CELLS + @  DUP ROT - RS-VARINT,
  LOOP DROP ;

\ ---- the special words ----------------------------------------------
\ xt -> handler ( arg --- ), compiling the word's code in its place; at
\ the build only.
1024 CONSTANT SP-BUCKETS
VARIABLE SP-TAB   0 SP-TAB !
: SP-BUCKET ( xt --- a-addr )  3 RSHIFT SP-BUCKETS 1- AND CELLS SP-TAB @ + ;
: SPECIAL ( xt handler arg --- )                  \ [next][xt][handler][arg]
  SP-TAB @ 0= IF 2DROP DROP EXIT THEN
  4 CELLS SP-ALLOT                                ( xt h arg e )
  TUCK 3 CELLS + !  TUCK 2 CELLS + !              ( xt e )
  2DUP CELL+ !  SWAP SP-BUCKET  2DUP @ SWAP !  ! ;
: SPECIAL? ( xt --- entry | 0 )
  SP-TAB @ 0= IF DROP 0 EXIT THEN
  DUP SP-BUCKET @
  BEGIN DUP WHILE  2DUP CELL+ @ = IF NIP EXIT THEN  @  REPEAT NIP ;

: NOOPS> ( c-addr --- c-addr' )  8 0 DO DUP C@ IF LEAVE THEN 1+ LOOP ;
' START NOOPS> C@ CONSTANT DOVAR-OP              \ a kernel variable's: DOVAR, after its NOOPs
: DOVAR? ( xt --- 0 | 1 | 2 )   \ a variable's code: ours 1, the kernel's 2 - DOVAR after the
  \ NOOPs where the converter aligned it (on a JIT design ours begin with the JIT's header instead)
  DUP C@ DOVAR-BYTE = IF DROP 1 EXIT THEN  NOOPS> C@ DOVAR-OP = 2 AND ;
\ A call through EXECUTE (I-EXEC): for a design whose JIT (the gene
\ jitexec) translates a word only if it translates every word the word
\ calls, and runs EXECUTE's word from native code - native if it could
\ translate it, the interpreter if not; the call site keeps it in a cache.
: I-EXEC ( xt --- )  REL-LITERAL ['] EXECUTE OLD-COMPILE, ;

\ ---- the JIT's depth (PORT-JIT 2) -------------------------------------
\ The JIT translates a word with every word below it, depth first, and gives
\ up 16 calls down (jit.c's JIT_DEPTH) - the word at the top then for good:
\ $(( )) is 21 calls deep from XE-TRY, and the five words above AE-EVAL
\ stayed interpreted. So each word's depth is kept, and a call that would
\ make a word deeper than DEP-MAX is made through EXECUTE instead: its word
\ is translated when it first runs, from the top. The kernel's words are
\ taken as 3 deep.
\   But not a call of a word that may THROW out of itself (a THROW in it, or
\ in a word it calls - not through EXECUTE or CATCH): the JIT's THROW in the
\ interpreter cannot unwind native code - it goes on in the innermost
\ interpreter, and the next return from a nested one lands in the wrong
\ frame. A word that calls THROW is never translated (THROW's own operations
\ have no stencils), nor is every word that calls it: so the parser's words,
\ the interpreter's, a forth command's stay interpreted from their CATCH to
\ their THROW - unless a call through EXECUTE made one above it native. Nor a
\ word that reads its caller's return address (an R> or R@ before any >R):
\ under EXECUTE it would find the JIT's.
12 CONSTANT DEP-MAX
VARIABLE DEP-TAB   0 DEP-TAB !                   \ buckets of [next][xt][depth][flags]
VARIABLE DEP-CUR                                 \ the definition's deepest callee so far
VARIABLE DEP-R                                   \ 1 its first R operation a >R, -1 an R> or R@
VARIABLE DEP-THR                                 \ it calls a word that may throw
\ flags: 1 may throw out of it, 2 reads its caller's return address
: DEP-BUCKET ( xt --- a-addr )  3 RSHIFT SP-BUCKETS 1- AND CELLS DEP-TAB @ + ;
: DEP-ENTRY ( xt --- entry | 0 )
  DUP DEP-BUCKET @
  BEGIN DUP WHILE  2DUP CELL+ @ = IF NIP EXIT THEN  @  REPEAT NIP ;
: DEP@ ( xt --- depth flags )
  DUP DEP-ENTRY ?DUP IF  NIP DUP 2 CELLS + @ SWAP 3 CELLS + @ EXIT  THEN
  PRIMITIVE? IF 0 ELSE 3 THEN 0 ;
: DEP! ( depth flags xt --- )
  4 CELLS SP-ALLOT  TUCK CELL+ !  TUCK 3 CELLS + !  TUCK 2 CELLS + !
  DUP CELL+ @ DEP-BUCKET  2DUP @ SWAP !  ! ;
: DEP-THROWS ( xt --- )  3 1 ROT DEP! ;          \ a seed: the kernel's THROW, ABORT ...
VARIABLE DEP-TOR   VARIABLE DEP-FROMR   VARIABLE DEP-RFETCH   \ the xts of >R R> R@
: DEP-RSTACK ( xt --- )   \ an R> or R@ before any >R: the caller's return address
  DEP-R @ IF DROP EXIT THEN                       \ decided
  DUP DEP-TOR @ = IF DROP 1 DEP-R ! EXIT THEN
  DUP DEP-FROMR @ =  SWAP DEP-RFETCH @ =  OR IF -1 DEP-R ! THEN ;
: DEP-CALL ( xt --- )   \ compile a call - or a primitive - minding the depth
  DUP PRIMITIVE? IF DUP DEP-RSTACK OLD-COMPILE, EXIT THEN
  DUP DEP@                                        ( xt d f )
  DUP 1 AND IF 1 DEP-THR ! THEN
  0= OVER DEP-MAX < 0= AND IF  DROP I-EXEC EXIT  THEN   \ deep, and safe through EXECUTE
  DEP-CUR @ MAX DEP-CUR !  OLD-COMPILE, ;
: DEP-BEGIN ( --- )  0 DEP-CUR !  0 DEP-R !  0 DEP-THR ! ;
: DEP-END ( xt --- )   \ the definition just ended
  DEP-TAB @ 0= IF DROP EXIT THEN
  >R  DEP-CUR @ 1+  DEP-THR @  DEP-R @ 0< IF 2 OR THEN  R> DEP! ;
: DEP-SAFE? ( xt --- f )   \ may be called through EXECUTE: neither flag
  DEP-TAB @ 0= IF DROP -1 EXIT THEN  DEP@ NIP 0= ;

: COMPILE, ( xt --- )
  REL-ON @ 0= IF OLD-COMPILE, EXIT THEN
  DUP SPECIAL? ?DUP IF  NIP DUP 3 CELLS + @ SWAP 2 CELLS + @ EXECUTE EXIT  THEN
  VAR-LIT @ IF DUP DOVAR? VAR-LIT @ AND IF  EXECUTE REL-LITERAL EXIT  THEN THEN
  DEP-TAB @ IF DEP-CALL EXIT THEN
  OLD-COMPILE, ;

\ ---- the inliner ----------------------------------------------------
\ interp.4's INTERPRET tells it each token of a definition: a word it
\ compiles (INL-XT), a number (INL-LIT), an immediate word it runs (INL-IMM:
\ the end of it, but for ;). ; then registers a definition of 1 to INL-MAX
\ tokens. Not one that touches the return stack.
4 CONSTANT INL-MAX
VARIABLE INL-N   -1 INL-N !                       \ tokens so far; -1, not a candidate
VARIABLE INL-LAST                                 \ LAST when it began
CREATE INL-TOK  INL-MAX 2 * CELLS ALLOT           \ [type][value]: 0 a word, 1 a number
CREATE INL-SAFE  4 CELLS ALLOT  INL-SAFE 4 CELLS 0 FILL   \ immediate words that compile
                                                  \ nothing of their own: ( \ and the ; words
VARIABLE INL-BAD     0 INL-BAD !                  \ [n][xt ...]: the return stack's words
: INL-BREAK ( --- )  -1 INL-N ! ;
: STR-EQ0? ( c-addr1 u1 c-addr2 u2 --- f )   \ the build's: names
  ROT OVER <> IF DROP 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN
  0 ?DO OVER I + C@ OVER I + C@ <> IF 2DROP 0 UNLOOP EXIT THEN LOOP 2DROP -1 ;
: INL-START ( --- )  REL-ON @ IF LAST @ INL-LAST !  0 INL-N ! ELSE INL-BREAK THEN ;
: INL-REC ( value type --- )
  INL-N @ 0< IF 2DROP EXIT THEN
  INL-N @ INL-MAX < 0= IF 2DROP INL-BREAK EXIT THEN
  INL-TOK INL-N @ 2 * CELLS +  TUCK !  CELL+ !  1 INL-N +! ;
: INL-BAD? ( xt --- f )
  INL-BAD @ ?DUP 0= IF DROP 0 EXIT THEN
  DUP @ 0 ?DO  DUP I 1+ CELLS + @ 2 PICK = IF 2DROP -1 UNLOOP EXIT THEN  LOOP 2DROP 0 ;
: INL-XT ( xt --- xt )  DUP INL-BAD? IF INL-BREAK ELSE DUP 0 INL-REC THEN ;
: INL-LIT ( x --- x )  DUP 1 INL-REC ;
: INL-SAFE! ( xt --- )   \ one more (after.4: shadow.4's ;)
  4 0 DO INL-SAFE I CELLS + @ 0= IF INL-SAFE I CELLS + ! UNLOOP EXIT THEN LOOP DROP ;
: INL-IMM ( xt --- xt )
  4 0 DO DUP INL-SAFE I CELLS + @ = IF UNLOOP EXIT THEN LOOP  INL-BREAK ;
: I-INLINE ( block --- )   \ the tokens again, each through COMPILE,
  DUP @ 0 ?DO
    DUP I 2 * 1+ CELLS +  DUP CELL+ @ SWAP @ IF REL-LITERAL ELSE COMPILE, THEN
  LOOP DROP ;
: INL-COMMIT ( --- )
  INL-N @ DUP 0> SWAP INL-MAX 1+ < AND  LAST @ INL-LAST @ = AND IF
    INL-N @ 2 * 1+ CELLS SP-ALLOT                 ( block )
    INL-N @ OVER !
    INL-TOK OVER CELL+ INL-N @ 2 * CELLS MOVE
    LAST @ NAME> ['] I-INLINE ROT SPECIAL
  THEN INL-BREAK ;
\ OVERRIDE ( xt "name" --- ): a definition of name, when it ends, has its
\ calls compiled as calls to xt - one that does the same (after.4).
VARIABLE OVR-LIST   0 OVR-LIST !                 \ [next][xt][count+name], the build's
: OVERRIDE ( xt "name" --- )
  SP-HP @ 0= IF DROP BL WORD DROP EXIT THEN
  BL WORD DUP C@ 1+ 2 CELLS + SP-ALLOT            ( xt name e )
  OVR-LIST @ OVER !  DUP OVR-LIST !  ROT OVER CELL+ !
  2 CELLS + OVER C@ 1+ MOVE ;
: I-CALL ( xt --- )  COMPILE, ;
\ EXEC-NAME ( "name" --- ): a definition of name, when it ends, has its
\ calls compiled as xt EXECUTE - on a design whose JIT (the gene jitexec)
\ translates a word only if it translates every word it calls, and EXECUTE
\ from native code runs a word it refused in the interpreter. So one word
\ the JIT cannot take (a system call, SP!, the return stack out of order)
\ no longer leaves every word above it interpreted. For words that are
\ cold or wait on the system anyway: the call costs an interpreter entry.
VARIABLE EXEC-LIST   0 EXEC-LIST !               \ [next][count+name], the build's
: EXEC-XT ( xt --- )  ['] I-EXEC OVER SPECIAL ;
: EXEC-NAME ( "name" --- )   \ on a jitexec design (PORT-JIT 2) only
  SP-HP @ 0=  PORT-JIT @ 2 = 0=  OR IF BL WORD DROP EXIT THEN
  BL WORD DUP C@ 1+ CELL+ SP-ALLOT                 ( name e )
  EXEC-LIST @ OVER !  DUP EXEC-LIST !  CELL+ OVER C@ 1+ MOVE ;
: LAST-NAMED? ( entry-name --- f )  COUNT  LAST @ COUNT 31 AND  STR-EQ0? ;
: OVR-CHECK ( --- )   \ the definition just ended
  REL-ON @ 0= IF EXIT THEN
  EXEC-LIST @ BEGIN ?DUP WHILE
    DUP CELL+ LAST-NAMED? IF  DROP LAST @ NAME> DUP DEP-SAFE? IF EXEC-XT ELSE DROP THEN EXIT  THEN @
  REPEAT
  OVR-LIST @ BEGIN ?DUP WHILE
    DUP 2 CELLS + LAST-NAMED? IF
      LAST @ NAME> ['] I-CALL ROT CELL+ @ SPECIAL EXIT
    THEN @
  REPEAT ;
: : ( "name" --- )  :  INL-START DEP-BEGIN ;
: ; ( --- )  POSTPONE ;  LAST @ NAME> DEP-END  INL-COMMIT OVR-CHECK ; IMMEDIATE
' ; INL-SAFE!  ' ( INL-SAFE!  ' \ INL-SAFE!

\ ---- the kernel's small words, inline -------------------------------
\ Each the kernel's own definition (forth-vm-evolution's forth/kernel.4),
\ its primitives compiled where the call was.
: LIT, ( x --- )  POSTPONE LITERAL ;
: I-CELLS   DROP CELL-SHIFT LIT, POSTPONE LSHIFT ;
: I-CELL+   DROP 1 CELLS LIT, POSTPONE + ;
: I-1+      DROP 1 LIT, POSTPONE + ;
: I-1-      DROP -1 LIT, POSTPONE + ;
: I--       DROP POSTPONE NEGATE POSTPONE + ;
: I-+!      DROP POSTPONE DUP POSTPONE @ POSTPONE ROT POSTPONE + POSTPONE SWAP POSTPONE ! ;
: I-2DROP   DROP POSTPONE DROP POSTPONE DROP ;
: I-2DUP    DROP POSTPONE OVER POSTPONE OVER ;
: I-?DUP    DROP POSTPONE DUP POSTPONE IF POSTPONE DUP POSTPONE THEN ;
: I-PICK    DROP 1 LIT, POSTPONE + CELL-SHIFT LIT, POSTPONE LSHIFT POSTPONE SP@ POSTPONE + POSTPONE @ ;
: I-0<      DROP 0 LIT, POSTPONE < ;
: I-0=      DROP 0 LIT, POSTPONE = ;
: I-0>      DROP 0 LIT, POSTPONE SWAP POSTPONE < ;
: I->       DROP POSTPONE SWAP POSTPONE < ;
: I-U>      DROP POSTPONE SWAP POSTPONE U< ;
: I-<>      DROP POSTPONE = 0 LIT, POSTPONE = ;
: I-0<>     DROP 0 LIT, POSTPONE = 0 LIT, POSTPONE = ;
: I-MIN     DROP POSTPONE OVER POSTPONE OVER POSTPONE SWAP POSTPONE < POSTPONE IF POSTPONE SWAP POSTPONE THEN POSTPONE DROP ;
: I-MAX     DROP POSTPONE OVER POSTPONE OVER POSTPONE < POSTPONE IF POSTPONE SWAP POSTPONE THEN POSTPONE DROP ;
: I-INVERT  DROP -1 LIT, POSTPONE XOR ;
: I-ABS     DROP POSTPONE DUP 0 LIT, POSTPONE < POSTPONE IF POSTPONE NEGATE POSTPONE THEN ;
: I-S>D     DROP POSTPONE DUP 0 LIT, POSTPONE < ;
: I-COUNT   DROP POSTPONE DUP 1 LIT, POSTPONE + POSTPONE SWAP POSTPONE C@ ;
: I-ALIGNED DROP 1 CELLS 1- LIT, POSTPONE + 1 CELLS NEGATE LIT, POSTPONE AND ;
: I-2SWAP   DROP POSTPONE ROT POSTPONE >R POSTPONE ROT POSTPONE R> ;
: I-NIP     DROP POSTPONE SWAP POSTPONE DROP ;
: I-TUCK    DROP POSTPONE SWAP POSTPONE OVER ;
: I-@XT     DROP POSTPONE @  ['] START COMPILE, POSTPONE @ POSTPONE + ;
: I-!XT     DROP POSTPONE SWAP ['] START COMPILE, POSTPONE @ POSTPONE NEGATE POSTPONE + POSTPONE SWAP POSTPONE ! ;
: I-*       DROP POSTPONE UM* POSTPONE DROP ;
: I-2*      DROP 1 LIT, POSTPONE LSHIFT ;
: I-CELL-   DROP 1 CELLS NEGATE LIT, POSTPONE + ;
: I-CONST   REL-LITERAL ;                         \ a constant: its value
: INLINE ( xt "name" --- )  ' SWAP 0 SPECIAL ;     \ name's calls compiled by xt

: COMPILE-INIT ( --- )   \ the build's tables (SPECIAL does nothing without them)
  REL-OK @ 0= IF EXIT THEN
  4194304 DUP ALLOCATE ABORT" compile.4: no memory" DUP SP-HP ! + SP-END !
  RS-MAX CELLS SP-ALLOT RS-TAB !  0 RS-N !
  SP-BUCKETS CELLS SP-ALLOT SP-TAB !  SP-TAB @ SP-BUCKETS CELLS 0 FILL
  7 CELLS SP-ALLOT INL-BAD !  6 INL-BAD @ !
  ['] >R INL-BAD @ CELL+ !  ['] R> INL-BAD @ 2 CELLS + !  ['] R@ INL-BAD @ 3 CELLS + !
  ['] I INL-BAD @ 4 CELLS + !  ['] RP@ INL-BAD @ 5 CELLS + !  ['] EXIT INL-BAD @ 6 CELLS + !
  ['] >R DEP-TOR !  ['] R> DEP-FROMR !  ['] R@ DEP-RFETCH !
  PORT-JIT @ 2 = IF  SP-BUCKETS CELLS SP-ALLOT DEP-TAB !  DEP-TAB @ SP-BUCKETS CELLS 0 FILL
    ['] THROW DEP-THROWS  ['] ABORT DEP-THROWS  ['] (ABORT") DEP-THROWS  ['] (THROW) DEP-THROWS  THEN ;
: COMPILE-OFF ( --- )   \ PORT-BOOT's, after RELOCATE: the tables were the build's
  0 REL-ON !  0 REL-REC !  0 VAR-LIT !  0 SP-TAB !  0 RS-TAB !  0 RS-N !  0 SP-HP !  0 SP-END !
  0 DEP-TAB !
  0 INL-BAD !  INL-BREAK ;

\ CONSTANT: its children's values compiled in place of their calls
: CONSTANT ( x "name" --- )
  DUP >R CONSTANT R>  LAST @ NAME> ['] I-CONST ROT SPECIAL ;

COMPILE-INIT
' I-CELLS INLINE CELLS      ' I-CELL+ INLINE CELL+    ' I-1+ INLINE 1+
' I-1+ INLINE CHAR+         ' I-1- INLINE 1-          ' I-- INLINE -
' I-+! INLINE +!            ' I-2DROP INLINE 2DROP    ' I-2DUP INLINE 2DUP
' I-?DUP INLINE ?DUP        ' I-PICK INLINE PICK      ' I-0< INLINE 0<
' I-0= INLINE 0=            ' I-0> INLINE 0>          ' I-> INLINE >
' I-U> INLINE U>            ' I-<> INLINE <>          ' I-0<> INLINE 0<>
' I-MIN INLINE MIN          ' I-MAX INLINE MAX        ' I-INVERT INLINE INVERT
' I-ABS INLINE ABS          ' I-S>D INLINE S>D        ' I-COUNT INLINE COUNT
' I-ALIGNED INLINE ALIGNED  ' I-2SWAP INLINE 2SWAP    ' I-NIP INLINE NIP
' I-TUCK INLINE TUCK        ' I-@XT INLINE @XT        ' I-!XT INLINE !XT
' I-* INLINE *              ' I-2* INLINE 2*          ' I-CELL- INLINE CELL-
' FALSE ' I-CONST 0 SPECIAL

\ POSTPONE: the kernel's compiles a word that is not immediate with its own
\ COMPILE, - a macro's words were not this front end's (pool.4's
\ BUFFER-BODY compiled a call to START, shadow.4's frames calls). This one
\ compiles it with COMPILE, here; the word is an offset, as the kernel's.
: (POSTPONE') ( --- )  R> DUP DUP @ + SWAP CELL+ >R  COMPILE, ;
: POSTPONE ( "name" --- )
  32 WORD FIND DUP 0= ABORT" Not found"
  1 = IF COMPILE, ELSE POSTPONE (POSTPONE') HERE - , THEN ; IMMEDIATE
REL-OK @ REL-ON !                    \ on: macros, constants, the inliner

\ RELOCATE runs before its sites are right, so it is compiled with its
\ variables called, not literals: on, but VAR-LIT off. Its state on the stack.
\ And START is not called either: the image's place is RS-ANCHOR's less its
\ offset - a JIT takes our variable, not the kernel's (a NOOP and DOVAR).
CREATE RS-ANCHOR
VARIABLE RS-ANCHOR-OFF   RS-ANCHOR START @ - RS-ANCHOR-OFF !
: IMAGE-AT ( --- a-addr )  RS-ANCHOR RS-ANCHOR-OFF @ - ;
: RS-SLOW ( c-addr --- c-addr' u )    \ a varint of more than a byte
  0 0 ROT                                         ( u shift p )
  BEGIN DUP C@ >R 1+ ROT ROT                      ( p u shift )
    R@ 127 AND OVER LSHIFT ROT OR SWAP 7 +        ( p u' shift' )
    ROT R> 128 AND 0=                             ( u' shift' p f )
  UNTIL NIP SWAP ;
: RELOCATE ( --- )    \ PORT-BOOT's first: every site by START's change
  RS-IMG @ 0= IF EXIT THEN
  IMAGE-AT RS-START @ -  DUP 0= IF DROP EXIT THEN    ( d )
  IMAGE-AT RS-IMG @ +  DUP @ >R  CELL+  IMAGE-AT     ( d p at )
  R> 0 ?DO
    OVER C@ 128 AND IF  SWAP RS-SLOW ROT +  ELSE  OVER C@ + SWAP 1+ SWAP  THEN
    2 PICK OVER +!
  LOOP 2DROP DROP
  IMAGE-AT RS-START ! ;

\ Variables as literals only where the build asks (PORT-VARLIT, build.sh's
\ VARLIT: 0 none, 1 all, 2 the kernel's): every design's LIT64 reads its
\ eight bytes one at a time, which costs more than the call and DOVAR it
\ saves. A JIT makes a call of our variable a literal itself (its header
\ says DOVAR), not of the kernel's (a NOOP first): so on a JIT design the
\ kernel's only - an image and a list of sites smaller by a third.
\ VAR-LIT: 1 ours, 2 the kernel's, 3 both (DOVAR?'s).
REL-OK @ PORT-VARLIT @ DUP 1 = 2 AND + AND VAR-LIT !  REL-OK @ REL-REC !   \ to the save

\ On a design with jitexec (PORT-JIT 2): the words its JIT cannot take that
\ the port and the shell call, through EXECUTE - the kernel's ALLOCATE FREE
\ RESIZE (a system call under them); the primitives the probes below find
\ (the system call, SCAN); and by name the words with SP! or the return
\ stack out of order, the I/O ones and the shell's few, each if it may not
\ throw. jitwords.4 adds an error's message, (ABORT-MSG), after interp.4:
\ there its errors are a forth command's, which a CATCH takes.
: ?EXEC-XT ( xt --- )  PORT-JIT @ 2 = IF EXEC-XT ELSE DROP THEN ;
: JIT-EXECS ( --- )
  ['] ALLOCATE ?EXEC-XT  ['] FREE ?EXEC-XT  ['] RESIZE ?EXEC-XT ;
JIT-EXECS
\ And the primitives a JIT may have no stencil for - which, a design's
\ genes say (best-all-round's CMOVE is C, X_CMOVE; fastest-x86-64's Forth):
\ each probed by a word that calls it past a false flag, run once here, so
\ the JIT translates it or refuses it. Refused, the primitive is called
\ through EXECUTE. A JIT header's four bytes follow its first byte: the
\ native code's offset once translated, 0 once refused.
: HDR@ ( a --- u )   \ four bytes, the low first
  DUP C@  OVER 1+ C@ 8 LSHIFT OR  OVER 2 + C@ 16 LSHIFT OR  SWAP 3 + C@ 24 LSHIFT OR ;
: JIT-NATIVE? ( xt --- f )  1+ HDR@  DUP 1 U>  SWAP 2147483648 AND 0=  AND ;
: ?ROUTE ( probe prim --- )
  PORT-JIT @ 2 = 0= IF 2DROP EXIT THEN
  SWAP DUP EXECUTE JIT-NATIVE? IF DROP ELSE EXEC-XT THEN ;
: P-SYSCALL 0 IF SYSCALL THEN ;   : P-SCAN 0 IF SCAN THEN ;   : P-FILL 0 IF FILL THEN ;
: P-CMOVE 0 IF CMOVE THEN ;   : P-CMOVE> 0 IF CMOVE> THEN ;
' P-SYSCALL ' SYSCALL ?ROUTE   ' P-SCAN ' SCAN ?ROUTE   ' P-FILL ' FILL ?ROUTE
' P-CMOVE ' CMOVE ?ROUTE   ' P-CMOVE> ' CMOVE> ?ROUTE
EXEC-NAME LOCALS-FAILED   EXEC-NAME READ-SOME   EXEC-NAME READ-FILE   EXEC-NAME READ-LINE
EXEC-NAME WRITE-FILE   EXEC-NAME FILE-MODE   EXEC-NAME REFILL-STDIN   EXEC-NAME RUN-CAUGHT
EXEC-NAME TEST-PARSE-INT   EXEC-NAME EXPAND-AND-RUN   EXEC-NAME EXEC-LOOP   EXEC-NAME RUN-TRAP
EXEC-NAME SHELL-PARSE-ARGS
BASE !
